allocate ff->release_args only if release is needed") skipped allocating ff->release_args when the FUSE server does not implement open. This caused fuse_prepare_release() to not grab a reference on the inode. As a result, an inode could be evicted from the dcache while there are inflight readahead requests. If the server triggers reclaim while servicing a readahead request, reclaim attempts to evict the inode, but the folio is locked during readahead. The eviction calls truncate_inode_pages_range() which tries to lock the folio, leading to a deadlock because readahead cannot release the lock as it is blocked in reclaim.

